# SSH options for the Zify deploy. inventory.py points at this file, and
# pyinfra reads it through paramiko's ssh_config support.
#
# ServerAliveInterval is the one that matters here. Without keepalives the SSH
# connection goes quiet while pyinfra waits at the "Detected changes" prompt,
# and anything in between - a home router's NAT table, a VPN, a local firewall -
# is free to drop it. The next command then fails with:
#
#   [WinError 10053] An established connection was aborted by the software in
#   your host machine
#
# Only ServerAliveInterval and ConnectTimeout are read from here; other ssh
# options are ignored, so connection settings belong in inventory.py instead.

Host *
    ServerAliveInterval 15
    ConnectTimeout 30
